The '''1934 FIFA World Cup final''' was the second edition of the [[Association football|football]] quadrennial tournament match contested by the men's national teams of [[FIFA]] to determine the [[1934 FIFA World Cup]] champions: [[Italy national football team|Italy]] and [[Czechoslovakia national football team|Czechoslovakia]]. It took place on 10 June 1934 at the [[Stadio Nazionale PNF]] in [[Rome]], Italy. 

After going a goal down, Italy came back to win the match 2–1 despite temperatures approaching {{convert|40|°C}}.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Kelly|first1=Jon|title=What happened to the Qatar World Cup's cooling technology?|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-31608062|access-date=4 June 2015|publisher=[[BBC]]|date=25 February 2015|archive-date=29 May 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150529115530/http://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-31608062|url-status=live}}</ref>

The last surviving player from that final was Czechoslovakia goalkeeper [[František Plánička]] who died on 20 July 1996 at the age of 92.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://zivot.cas.sk/clanok/788/frantisek-planicka-slavny-brankar-chytal-aj-so-zlomenym-laktom|website=Život|title=František Plánička: Slávny brankár chytal aj so zlomeným lakt'om!|date=30 May 2009|access-date=11 July 2015|language=sk|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150714194035/http://zivot.cas.sk/clanok/788/frantisek-planicka-slavny-brankar-chytal-aj-so-zlomenym-laktom|archive-date=14 July 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref>

==Background==
[[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]] boycotted the 1934 edition due to the lack of European teams in the [[1930 FIFA World Cup|previous tournament]] and [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] was eliminated in the first round of the tournament by [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]],<ref>{{cite book | last=Freddi| first=Cris|year=2006| title=Complete Book of the World Cup 2006| publisher=HarperCollins|location=London|isbn=0-00-722916-X|page=20}}</ref> assured that a previous team would not be defending their title.

This was the debut for each of the finalists in the [[FIFA World Cup]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/55/171012-statisticalkit-fifaworldcup-milestonesfactsfigures-statusafterfwc2010.pdf |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130521092116/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/55/171012-statisticalkit-fifaworldcup-milestonesfactsfigures-statusafterfwc2010.pdf |archive-date=21 May 2013 |publisher=[[FIFA]] |title=FIFA World Cup: Milestones, facts & figures. Statistical Kit 7 |date=26 March 2013}}</ref> This was the eleventh contest between the two teams, their immediate previous match being at the [[1933–35 Central European International Cup]] held in [[Florence]], [[Italy]]; Italy prevailed 2–0. This leveled the head-to-head in the World Cup match to three all with four draws.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablesi/itatsjres.html|title=Italy-Czech Republic/Czechoslovakia matches 1922-2013|date=21 December 2017|access-date=20 April 2019|archive-date=28 November 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221128141045/https://www.rsssf.org/tablesi/itatsjres.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

